{
  "original_id": "primary-20260914-grid-narayana",
  "archive_id": "BW2-PR20260914-grid_narayana",
  "title": "A Narayana factorization for a truncated two-row grid polytope",
  "batch_label": "primary",
  "kind": "resolution-paper",
  "original_status": "proved",
  "scope": "For every integer n>=1, let P_n=({1,...,n} x {1,2}) minus {(n,2)}, ordered coordinatewise, and Q_n={x>=0: sum_{v in I}x_v<=|I| for every lower ideal I of P_n}. Then sum_{x in Q_n intersect Z^(2n-1)} t^(number of nonzero coordinates of x) equals A_{n-1}(t) B_n(t), where A_r(t)=sum_{j=0}^r binom(r,j)binom(r+1,j)t^j/(j+1) and B_r(t)=sum_{j=0}^r binom(r,j)^2 t^j. This is the entire frozen original claim, with no change of statistic, hypotheses, or parameter range.",
  "gate_basis": "Current released terminal, manifest, PDF, TeX freeze, snapshot files, provenance and four audits agree.",
